# Everything here is excluded from the build context — the tarball uploaded to
# the builder on every `fly deploy`.
#
# This matters more than it looks. The repository is ~390 MB, and 198 MB of that
# is node_modules, which the image installs itself from package-lock.json. A
# further 16 MB is dist/, which the image rebuilds. Without this file every
# deploy would upload roughly 390 MB to build a site that needs about 15 MB of
# source.

# Installed by the image itself, from the lock file
**/node_modules

# Rebuilt inside the image
**/dist

# Design mockups and comparison boards — reference material, not the site
content/

# Local tooling: the double-click launchers, their README, the stale
# single-page snapshot, and an old archive
*.cmd
README-RUNNING.md
crimsonacademy-preview.html
*.zip

# Version control and editor state
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store

# Other hosts' config — irrelevant inside the container
netlify.toml

# Build caches and logs
**/.vite
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*
